I believe using [`FuturesUnordered`](https://docs.rs/futures/latest/futures/prelude/stream/struct.FuturesUnordered.html) is the recommended way to wait on a bunch of things at once without caring about ordering.

`spawn(async { x.await })` is also the same as just `spawn(x)`

```suggestion
    let clients = (0..N_CLIENTS)
        .into_iter()
        .map(|cli| tokio::spawn(spawn_client(cli)))
        .collect::<FuturesUnordered<_>>();

    //wait for all our clients to exit
    while clients.next().await.is_some() {}
```

